# Deliberately empty of rules.
#
# frontend/.gitignore excludes "dist", and npm falls back to .gitignore when a
# directory has no .npmignore. That would strip the prebuilt UI from the
# published tarball, leaving the CLI with nothing to serve. This file exists to
# shadow it; what actually gets published is the "files" whitelist in
# package.json, which only lets frontend/dist through.
